<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="994deb25-39f3-4a0b-aab6-1e0b86520581" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="5f4f2259-2fef-4583-987d-86e9687e8b43" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="The graph will be shifted 3 units to the right." data-solution-options="[&quot;The graph will be shifted 3 units down.&quot;, &quot;The graph will be shifted 3 units up.&quot;, &quot;The graph will be stretched vertically by a factor of 3.&quot;, &quot;The graph will be compressed vertically by a factor of 3.&quot;, &quot;The graph will be shifted 3 units to the right.&quot;, &quot;The graph will be shifted 3 units to the left.&quot;, &quot;The graph will be stretched horizontally by a factor of 3.&quot;, &quot;The graph will be compressed horizontally by a factor of 3.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>How will the graph of k(x) = x be affected if the transformation k(x - 3) is applied?</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The graph will be shifted 3 units to the right. This happens because the transformation \(k(x-3)\) moves the graph horizontally to the right by 3 units.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Think about how subtracting from the variable inside the function affects the graph’s position on the horizontal axis.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
